 "standard_text": "Recall and demonstrate proficiency with multiplication facts up to 10 x 10 and related division facts; extend and apply facts to develop efficient mental strategies for computation with larger numbers without a calculator",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 4 maths worksheets on multiplication facts to 10 × 10: the 6, 7, 8 and 9 times tables, related division facts, mental strategies, facts with zeros like 6 × 40, and word problems. 100 questions with an answer key, following the Australian Curriculum.",
 "key_big": "Use a fact you know to find one you don’t.",
 "key_sub": "Double the 3s for the 6s, double three times for the 8s, and for the 9s use the 10s and take away one group: 9 × 7 = 70 − 7 = 63. Every fact gives division facts and facts with zeros: 56 ÷ 8 = 7 and 7 × 80 = 560.",
 "body_html": "<h2>Know every fact to 10 × 10</h2><p>In Year 4 you learn all the multiplication facts up to 10 × 10. You already know the 2s, 3s, 4s, 5s and 10s. Turnarounds mean you know most of the rest too: 6 × 4 is the same as 4 × 6. The new facts to learn are the 6s, 7s, 8s and 9s.</p><figure class='sn-fig'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 166 144' width='166' height='144' role='img' aria-label='array of 6 rows with 7 dots in each row'><g font-family='Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif'><circle cx='17' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='127' r='7' fill='#006633'/></g></svg><figcaption>6 rows of 7: 7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42. 6 × 7 = 42.</figcaption></figure><h2>A trick for each fact family</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Facts</th><th>Trick</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>× 6</td><td>Double the 3s</td><td>6 × 7: 3 × 7 = 21, double = 42</td></tr><tr><td>× 7</td><td>5s + 2s</td><td>7 × 8: 40 + 16 = 56</td></tr><tr><td>× 8</td><td>Double, double, double</td><td>8 × 6: 12, 24, 48</td></tr><tr><td>× 9</td><td>10s take away one group</td><td>9 × 7: 70 − 7 = 63</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class='sn-fig'><svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 258 176' width='258' height='176' role='img' aria-label='array of 7 rows with 8 dots split into 5 rows and 2 rows'><g font-family='Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif'><circle cx='17' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='171' cy='17' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='171' cy='39' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='171' cy='61' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='171' cy='83' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='39' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='61' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='83' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='105' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='127' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='149' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='171' cy='105' r='7' fill='#006633'/><circle cx='17' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='39' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='61' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='83' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='105' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='127' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='149' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='171' cy='137' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='17' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='39' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='61' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='83' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='105' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='127' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='149' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><circle cx='171' cy='159' r='7' fill='#b5651d'/><line x1='6' y1='121.0' x2='182' y2='121.0' stroke='#2b2b2b' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='5 4'/><text x='190.0' y='67.0' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#006633' text-anchor='start'>5 × 8</text><text x='190.0' y='154.0' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#b5651d' text-anchor='start'>2 × 8</text></g></svg><figcaption>7 × 8 = 5 × 8 + 2 × 8 = 40 + 16 = 56.</figcaption></figure><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th></th><th>6s</th><th>7s</th><th>8s</th><th>9s</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>6</td><td>7</td><td>8</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>12</td><td>14</td><td>16</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>18</td><td>21</td><td>24</td><td>27</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>24</td><td>28</td><td>32</td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>30</td><td>35</td><td>40</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>36</td><td>42</td><td>48</td><td>54</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>42</td><td>49</td><td>56</td><td>63</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>48</td><td>56</td><td>64</td><td>72</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>54</td><td>63</td><td>72</td><td>81</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>60</td><td>70</td><td>80</td><td>90</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>9 × 6 = ?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>10 × 6 = 60. Take away one 6: 60 − 6 = 54.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 54</p></div><h2>Every fact gives division facts</h2><p>Division is the inverse of multiplication. 7, 8 and 56 make a <b>fact family</b>: 7 × 8 = 56, 8 × 7 = 56, 56 ÷ 7 = 8 and 56 ÷ 8 = 7.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Division</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>63 ÷ 9 = ?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Think: 9 × ? = 63. 9 × 7 = 63.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 7</p></div><h2>Facts with zeros</h2><p>Use the fact you know, then think in tens. 6 × 4 = 24, so 6 × 40 = 24 tens = 240.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Multiply</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>6 × 40 = ?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>6 × 4 = 24. 6 × 4 tens = 24 tens.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 240</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Divide</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>240 ÷ 8 = ?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>240 is 24 tens. 24 ÷ 8 = 3, so 24 tens ÷ 8 = 3 tens.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 30</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Word problem</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Sausages come in packets of 8. How many sausages are in 7 packets?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>7 packets of 8: 7 × 8 = 56.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 56 sausages</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mixing up 7 × 8 = 54 and 6 × 9 = 54</td><td>Say 5, 6, 7, 8: 56 = 7 × 8</td></tr><tr><td>Adding instead: 6 × 9 = 15</td><td>× means groups of: 6 groups of 9 = 54</td></tr><tr><td>9s trick: 10 × 7 − 1 = 69</td><td>Take away a whole group: 70 − 7 = 63</td></tr><tr><td>Dropping the zero: 6 × 40 = 24</td><td>6 × 4 tens = 24 tens = 240</td></tr><tr><td>Checking 56 ÷ 8 = 7 with 56 − 8</td><td>Check with multiplication: 7 × 8 = 56</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What multiplication facts should a Year 4 student know in Australia?",
   "a": "The Australian Curriculum (v9.0) asks Year 4 students to recall all multiplication facts up to 10 × 10 and the related division facts, such as 7 × 8 = 56 and 56 ÷ 8 = 7. They also use these facts for larger numbers, like 6 × 40 = 240."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do Year 4 students sit NAPLAN?",
   "a": "No. NAPLAN is for Years 3, 5, 7 and 9. Knowing every fact to 10 × 10 by the end of Year 4 gives students a strong start for the Year 5 numeracy test."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the easiest way to remember 7 × 8?",
   "a": "Say “5, 6, 7, 8”: 56 = 7 × 8. You can also split it: 5 × 8 = 40 and 2 × 8 = 16, so 7 × 8 = 40 + 16 = 56."
  },
  {
   "q": "How can I help my child learn the 6, 7, 8 and 9 times tables?",
   "a": "Teach one trick for each: double the 3s for the 6s, double three times for the 8s, and use the 10s and take away one group for the 9s. Practise a few facts each day and ask for the related division fact too."
  }
